.TH TULPAR-KEY 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.1.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-key \- manage the trusted signing keyring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar key add
.I key-path
.RI [ sig-path ]
.br
.B tulpar key list
.br
.B tulpar k
.I action
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B tulpar \-k
.I action
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages the trusted keyring used to verify package signatures.
.TP
.B add
Adds a new public key to the trusted keyring, if it is endorsed by a
key already present in the keyring.
.I sig-path
is the detached endorsement signature of the new key and is required
for the libsodium backend; it is ignored for the gpgme backend, whose
certifications are embedded in the key itself.
.TP
.B list
Prints the trusted keyring directory and the active signing backend.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-sign\-backend " sodium|gpgme"
Select which backend's keyring to operate on for this invocation.
Defaults to the
.I sign_backend
value from
.BR tulpar.conf (5).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the key was not added or the keyring could
not be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar.conf (5)
